Worktree: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/182-dispatch-lint-held-fixes (your current directory).
Spec folder: specs/cli-external-orchestration/082-opencode-v1-v2-dual-compat/040-dispatch-lint-held-fixes (pre-approved, skip Gate 3)

ROLE: Act as a code agent. Make one change: one shared helper and its four callers, plus tests.

Problem: each preflight adapter calls `resolveDispatchPacket(command)`, reads that ONE packet's hard rules and evaluates them. In `opencode run -m p/m "a" </dev/null && pi -p "b" </dev/null` the second dispatch's own packet rules (cli-pi's `--offline` rule, for one) are never evaluated. `resolveDispatchPackets(command)` in `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-audit.mjs` already returns every dispatch in order.

Fix:
1. In `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.mjs`, add and export `evaluateDispatch(command, skillsRoot, options = {})`. For each entry `resolveDispatchPackets(command)` returns, it reads `readHardRules(path.join(skillsRoot, entry.packetPath, 'SKILL.md'))`, skips a packet with no rules, runs `evaluate(command, rules, options)`, and collects `{ skill: entry.skill, violations }` for each packet with at least one violation, in command order. It returns that array (empty when nothing resolves or nothing is violated). JSDoc it in the file's style: every dispatch in a chain is held to its own packet's rules.
2. Use it in the four callers, keeping each one's own project-root and skills-root logic, its tool-name checks and its output format:
   - `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/claude/dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs`
   - `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs`
   - `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/devin/dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs`
   - `.opencode/plugins/cli-dispatch-audit.js` (the `tool.execute.before` hook only; it uses only blocking violations)
   Build the deny reason as one `Dispatch blocked by ${skill} hard-rule(s):` block per packet that has a blocking violation, joined by a newline, and the advisory as one `⚠ ${skill} dispatch hard-rule advisory:` block per packet that has warnings (the Claude, Codex and Devin adapters keep their existing advisory prefix). With one packet the output must be byte-for-byte what it is today. Remove imports that become unused.

Tests:
- In `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.test.mjs`, one `test(...)`: with `skillsRoot` the repository's `.skilled/skills` (resolve it from the test file's location the way the file already locates SKILL.md files), `evaluateDispatch('opencode run -m p/m "a" </dev/null && pi -p "b" </dev/null', skillsRoot)` returns an item for `cli-pi` whose violations include `pi-offline-required`; `evaluateDispatch('git status', skillsRoot)` returns `[]`.
- In `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/codex-shell-tool.test.mjs`, inside `describe('Codex dispatch preflight lint', ...)`, one `it` that sends `opencode run -m p/m "a" </dev/null && pi -p "b" </dev/null` through the lint hook with `cwd: REPO_ROOT` and asserts stdout contains `pi-offline-required`.
- Run the existing OpenCode plugin tests; if any asserts the old single-packet behaviour of `cli-dispatch-audit.js`, report it rather than weakening it.

Comments keep the durable WHY and never name spec paths, phases, or task, review or finding ids.

VERIFICATION (run each from the worktree root with node from /Users/michelkerkmeester/.nvm/versions/node/v26.8.2/bin on PATH; all must pass):
node --check .skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.mjs
node --check .opencode/plugins/cli-dispatch-audit.js
node --test .skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.test.mjs
.skilled/node_modules/.bin/vitest run --config .skilled/hooks/vitest.config.ts .skilled/hooks/dispatch/
node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/*.test.cjs

